[%title]: First part: what's a "system"?
[%series]: demo
[%description]: The first of two parts, with a note and some maths.

## The idea

A system maps an input $u$ to an output $y$, and it is linear if $y(au) = a\,y(u)$.[^scaling]

[^scaling]: Scaling the input scales the output, which is the first of two rules.

Two rules:

- Scaling
- Additivity
